#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:106
#, xml-text
msgid "Required"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:108
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<xref linkend=\"xorg7-lib\"/>, <xref linkend=\"libdrm\"/>, <xref "
"linkend=\"Mako\"/>, and <xref linkend=\"PyYAML\"/>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><bridgehead>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:114
#, xml-text
msgid "Recommended"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:120
#, xml-text
msgid "<xref linkend=\"glslang\"/> (required for Vulkan support)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:125
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<xref linkend=\"libva\"/> (to provide VA-API support for some gallium "
"drivers. Note that there is a circular dependency.  You must build "
"<application>libva</application> first without mesa's EGL and GLX support, "
"install this package, and rebuild <application>libva</application>)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:134
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<xref linkend=\"llvm\"/> (required for the llvmpipe, r300, r600, and "
"radeonsi drivers)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:140
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<xref linkend=\"wayland-protocols\"/> (required for <xref role=\"nodep\" "
"linkend='plasma-build'/>, GNOME, and recommended for <xref role=\"nodep\" "
"linkend='gtk3'/>)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:148
#, xml-text
msgid "<xref linkend=\"libclc\"/> (required for the Intel iris gallium driver)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:154
#, xml-text
msgid "<xref linkend=\"vulkan-loader\"/> (required for Vulkan support)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:159
#, xml-text
msgid "<xref linkend=\"ply\"/> (required for the Intel vulkan driver)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:164
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<xref linkend=\"cbindgen\"/>, <xref linkend=\"make-ca\"/>, and <xref "
"linkend=\"rust-bindgen\"/> (required for the Nouveau Vulkan driver)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:175
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"An Internet connection is needed for building the Nouveau Vulkan driver.  "
"The system certificate store may need to be set up with <xref "
"role='recommended' linkend='make-ca'/> before building this package."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:184
#, xml-text
msgid "<emphasis role=\"bold\">Choosing Mesa Drivers</emphasis>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:188
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"In the instructions below, all the available drivers are built.  That will "
"almost always work.  However, it is not efficient.  Depending on your video "
"hardware, you probably need only specific drivers."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:194
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"The first thing you need to know is which type of video device you have.  In"
" some cases it is built into the CPU.  In others it is a separate PCI card."
"  In either case you can tell what video hardware you have by installing "
"<xref linkend='pciutils'/> and running:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:200
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>lspci | grep VGA</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:203
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"The video device is most likely one of three families: AMD, Intel, or "
"NVIDIA.  See the Command Explanations for <parameter>-D gallium-"
"drivers=auto</parameter> below to see what options are available for your "
"specific video hardware (or emulated video hardware).  You should probably "
"add the softpipe or llvmpipe option as a backup driver."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:212
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"For 'platforms' you can select x11 and/or wayland.  Note that in BLFS "
"currently only Gnome and KDE can use wayland.  If you are not going to use "
"one of those desktop environments then you probably only want x11."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:218
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"For 'vulkan-drivers' you may want to limit the selection to your current "
"hardware.  These drivers are used by some specific applications.  For "
"example, ffmpeg (including ffplay) will use Vulkan instead of OpenGL for "
"rendering video on the GPU. If you do not want to do this you may or may not"
" want to install them.  See the Command Explanations for <parameter>-D "
"vulkan-drivers=auto</parameter> below to see what options are available for "
"your specific video hardware (or emulated video hardware).  You should "
"probably add the swrast option as a backup driver unless you don't need "
"Vulkan at all."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><bridgehead>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:232
#, xml-text
msgid "Optional"
msgstr ""

#.  for libsensors according to Meson
#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:234
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<xref linkend=\"libdisplay-info\"/>, <xref linkend=\"libgcrypt\"/>, <xref "
"linkend=\"libunwind\"/>, <xref linkend=\"lm_sensors\"/>, <xref "
"linkend=\"nettle\"/>, <xref linkend=\"valgrind\"/>, <ulink "
"url=\"https://archive.mesa3d.org/demos/\">mesa-demos</ulink> (provides more "
"than 300 extra demos to test <application>Mesa</application>; this includes "
"the same programs added by the patch above), <ulink "
"url=\"https://omxil.sourceforge.net/\">Bellagio OpenMAX Integration "
"Layer</ulink> (for mobile platforms), <ulink url=\"https://glfs-"
"book.github.io/glfs/shareddeps/libglvnd.html\">libglvnd</ulink> (provides "
"OpenGL libraries), and <ulink url=\"https://github.com/tizonia/tizonia-"
"openmax-il/wiki/Tizonia-OpenMAX-IL/\"> libtizonia</ulink>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Attribute 'xreflabel' of: <sect1><sect2>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:268
#, xml-text
msgid "Mesa Kernel Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:269
#, xml-text
msgid "Kernel Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:272
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Enable the following options in the kernel configuration and recompile the "
"kernel if necessary:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:281
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"The corresponding Mesa Gallium3D driver name is provided as the comment for "
"the configuration entries.  If you don't know the name of the Mesa Gallium3D"
" driver for your GPU, see <xref linkend=\"mesa-gallium-drivers\"/> below."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:288
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"For the GPUs supported by the Iris Gallium3D driver, with "
"<option>CONFIG_DRM_I915</option> enabled and "
"<option>CONFIG_DRM_XE_FORCE_PROBE</option> set to the string "
"<literal>*</literal>, the i915 driver will be used if it supports the GPU, "
"and the Xe driver will be used if it supports the GPU but the i915 driver "
"does not.  If you are sure your GPU is supported by the i915 driver, you can"
" disable the Xe driver to save some build time.  If your GPU is supported by"
" both drivers and you want to use the Xe driver, you can disable the i915 "
"driver, or make the i915 driver deny your GPU via the "
"<option>CONFIG_DRM_I915_FORCE_PROBE</option> option, for example setting it "
"to <literal>!7d55</literal> would make i915 deny the Meteor Lake integrated "
"GPU (of which the PCI ID is <literal>8086:7d55</literal>), leaving it for "
"the Xe driver."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:305
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<option>CONFIG_DRM_RADEON</option>, <option>CONFIG_DRM_AMDGPU</option>, "
"<option>CONFIG_DRM_NOUVEAU</option>, <option>CONFIG_DRM_I915</option>, and "
"<option>CONFIG_DRM_XE</option> may require firmware.  See <xref "
"linkend='postlfs-firmware'/> for details."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:314
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Selecting <option>CONFIG_DRM_RADEON</option>, "
"<option>CONFIG_DRM_AMDGPU</option>, or <option>CONFIG_DRM_NOUVEAU</option> "
"as <quote><literal>y</literal></quote> is not recommended. If it is, any "
"required firmware must be built as a part of the kernel image or the "
"initramfs for the driver to function correctly."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:323
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"The sub-entries under <option>CONFIG_DRM_AMDGPU</option> are used to ensure "
"the AMDGPU kernel driver supports all GPUs using the "
"<literal>radeonsi</literal> driver.  They are not needed if you won't need "
"<option>CONFIG_DRM_AMDGPU</option> itself. They may be unneeded for some GPU"
" models."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:331
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"For <literal>llvmpipe</literal> or <literal>softpipe</literal>, "
"<option>CONFIG_DRM_VGEM</option> is required or X clients may fail to start "
"with a cryptic message <computeroutput>Error: couldn't get an RGB, Double-"
"buffered visual</computeroutput>.  Strictly speaking, it can be compiled as "
"a module.  But the module will not be loaded automatically, so it's more "
"convenient to build it as a part of the kernel image."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><indexterm><primary>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:341
#, xml-text
msgid "mesa"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:346
#, xml-text
msgid "Installation of Mesa"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:348
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If you have downloaded the xdemos patch (needed if testing the Xorg "
"installation per BLFS instructions), apply it by running the following "
"command:"
msgstr ""

#. <screen>
#. <userinput>patch -Np1 -i ../mesa-&mesa-
#. version;-add_xdemos-1.patch</userinput></screen>
#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:354
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>patch -Np1 -i ../mesa-add_xdemos-4.patch</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:422
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Install <application>Mesa</application> by running the following commands:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:426
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>mkdir build &amp;&amp;\n"
"cd    build &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"meson setup ..                 \\\n"
"      --prefix=$XORG_PREFIX    \\\n"
"      --buildtype=release      \\\n"
"      -D platforms=x11,wayland \\\n"
"      -D gallium-drivers=auto  \\\n"
"      -D vulkan-drivers=auto   \\\n"
"      -D valgrind=disabled     \\\n"
"      -D video-codecs=all      \\\n"
"      -D libunwind=disabled   &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"ninja</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><warning><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:443
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Please ask your lawyer or remove the <parameter>-D video-"
"codecs=all</parameter> option if you will distribute the compiled Mesa "
"libraries and drivers to others."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:450
#, xml-text
msgid "To test the results, issue:"
msgstr ""

#. sed '/float rsqrtf/,/^}/d' \
#.     -i ../src/gallium/drivers/llvmpipe/lp_test_arit.c &amp;&amp;
#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:453
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>meson configure -D build-tests=true &amp;&amp;\n"
"ninja test</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:466
#, xml-text
msgid "Now, as the &root; user:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:469
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>ninja install</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:472
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If desired, install the optional documentation by running the following "
"commands as the &root; user:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:477
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>cp -rv ../docs -T /usr/share/doc/mesa-&mesa-version;</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:482
#, xml-text
msgid "Command Explanations"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:485
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<parameter>--buildtype=release</parameter>: This switch ensures a fully-"
"optimized build, and disables debug assertions which will severely slow down"
" the libraries in certain use-cases. Without this switch, build sizes can "
"span into the 2 GB range."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:492
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<anchor id='mesa-gallium-drivers' xreflabel='Mesa Gallium3D Drivers'/> "
"<parameter>-D gallium-drivers=auto</parameter>: This parameter controls "
"which Gallium3D drivers should be built:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:499
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<literal>auto</literal> selects all Gallium3D drivers available for x86. "
"With a comma-separated list, only a subset of these drivers will be built. "
"If you precisely know which drivers you need, you can select them "
"explicitly. For example, <option>-D gallium-"
"drivers=radeonsi,iris,llvmpipe</option>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:508
#, xml-text
msgid "<literal>r300</literal> (for ATI Radeon 9000 or Radeon X series)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:513
#, xml-text
msgid "<literal>r600</literal> (for AMD/ATI Radeon HD 2000-6000 series)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:518
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<literal>radeonsi</literal> (for AMD Radeon HD 7000 or newer AMD GPU models)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:523
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<literal>nouveau</literal> (for supported NVIDIA GPUs, they are listed as "
"all <quote>3D features</quote> either <quote>DONE</quote> or "
"<quote>N/A</quote> in <ulink "
"url='https://nouveau.freedesktop.org/FeatureMatrix.html'>the Nouveau status "
"page</ulink>)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:532
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<literal>virgl</literal> (for a QEMU virtual GPU with "
"<application>virglrender</application> support; note that BLFS <xref "
"linkend='qemu'/> is not built with <application>virglrender</application>)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:540
#, xml-text
msgid "<literal>svga</literal> (for a VMWare virtual GPU)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:545
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<literal>llvmpipe</literal> (using CPU for 3D rasterization. Note that it's "
"much slower than using a modern 3D-capable GPU, so it should be only used if"
" the GPU is not supported by other drivers)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:553
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<literal>softpipe</literal> (also using CPU for 3D rasterization, but slower"
" than llvmpipe. There is not much reason to use it unless LLVM is not "
"available)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:560
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<literal>iris</literal> (for Intel GPUs shipped with Broadwell or newer "
"CPUs, or as a dedicated PCIe card)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:566
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<literal>crocus</literal> (for Intel GMA 3000, X3000 series, 4000 series, or"
" X4000 series GPUs shipped with chipsets, or Intel HD GPUs shipped with pre-"
"Broadwell CPUs)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:573
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<literal>i915</literal> (for Intel GMA 900, 950, 3100, or 3150 GPUs shipped "
"with chipsets or Atom D/N 4xx/5xx CPUs)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:579
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<literal>zink</literal> (uses Vulkan to implement OpenGL, and while unstable"
" at times, it can be a decent replacement for non-performant gallium drivers"
" like nouveau)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:588
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<parameter>-D vulkan-drivers=auto</parameter>: This parameter controls which"
" Vulkan drivers should be built:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:594
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<literal>auto</literal> selects all Vulkan drivers available for x86. With a"
" comma-separated list, only a subset of these drivers will be built. If you "
"precisely know which drivers you need, you can select them explicitly. For "
"example, <option>-D vulkan-drivers=amd,nouveau,swrast</option>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:604
#, xml-text
msgid "<literal>amd</literal> (for AMD Radeon HD 7730 or newer AMD GPUs)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:610
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<literal>intel</literal> (for Intel GPUs shipped with Skylake or newer CPUs,"
" or as a dedicated PCIe card)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:617
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<literal>intel_hasvk</literal> (for Intel GPUs shipped with Ivy Bridge, "
"Haswell, or Broadwell CPUs)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:624
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<literal>nouveau</literal> (for GTX 16XX, RTX 20XX, or newer NVIDIA GPUs)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:631
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<literal>swrast</literal> (for using the CPU for 3D rasterization)  Note "
"that it's much slower than using a modern 3D-capable GPU, so it should be "
"only used if the GPU is not supported by other drivers."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:640
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<literal>\"\"</literal> (empty list, use <option>-D vulkan-"
"drivers=\"\"</option> if you've not installed and you don't plan to install "
"<xref linkend='vulkan-loader'/>)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:649
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<parameter>-D platforms=...</parameter>: This parameter controls which "
"windowing systems will be supported. Available linux platforms are x11 and "
"wayland."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:655
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<parameter>-D valgrind=disabled</parameter>: This parameter disables the "
"usage of Valgrind during the build process. Remove this parameter if you "
"have Valgrind installed, and wish to check for memory leaks."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:661
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<parameter>-D video-codecs=all</parameter>: This parameter enables building "
"codecs for video formats covered by third-party patents."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:666
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<parameter>-D libunwind=disabled</parameter>: This parameter disables the "
"usage of libunwind."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:671
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<command>meson configure -D build-tests=true</command>: This command will "
"reconfigure the build to set <option>-D build-tests=true</option>, but keep "
"the other options specified in the <command>meson setup</command> command "
"unchanged.  It allows <command>ninja test</command> to build and run unit "
"tests."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/x/installing/mesa.xml:679
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<option>-D egl-native-platform=\"...\"</option>: This parameter controls "
"which Embedded Graphics Library support will be built. Available linux "
"options are auto (default), x11, wayland, surfaceless, and drm."
msgstr ""

